{
  "about": "The store's waits family: the arrival log, wait rows and their newly-matches bits (docs/contracts/store-slot.md, `waits.*`). Held by listen-fire's stores: crates/lf/src/waits.rs runs every case over the SQLite state file, and over Postgres when LF_TEST_PG names one; apps/cli/src/__test__/store_slot.test.ts runs every case over the store slot's wire. Each case runs on an empty store. A run or team name stands for a fresh id (a uuid) per case; every run named is started before the first step, except those the case lists as `unstarted` (runs a delivery queued, started by `start`). `team` defaults to \"t\" and `adapter` to \"acme\". Marks and waits are named by `as` and referred to by that name. `at` and `before` are milliseconds from now. Steps: `mark` (waits.mark, kept as `as`); `log` (waits.log of `arrivals`, logged `at`, under the module's re-send window `resendWindowMs` (an hour when the step gives none); an arrival whose identity and version its record's edge logged within that window after it is not logged again, even after the sweep forgot its entry, and one without an identity is never a repeat; `wakes` the parked waits it answers, in any order; an arrival's `identityIsSeqOf` names a listed arrival whose seq, as bare text, is its identity; `queued`, when given, the `wake_await` rows due after the log, each `{ run, wait, address }` as its payload's `runId`, `waitId` and `address`, in any order: the log queues one per wait it answers, in its own write, and none twice. They are claimed as the step's team's drain claims them (work.claimDue of that kind, leasing them), so a later `queued` lists only the rows queued since; `stranded` the waits it leaves stranded, by name, in any order, none when absent: a gone arrival strands each wait parked on its record that is not stranded already, and any other arrival on a record clears the stranding of each of its waits, the newest report winning, within one log too); `open` (waits.open since the mark `since`, kept as `as`; `same` names an earlier wait it must be; without a `key`, a wait on a record already gone, one per run and edge as a keyed wait is one per record); `arrivals` (waits.arrivals: `arrivals` in log order, each checked on the keys it gives, and kept by the name its `as` gives); `note` (waits.note, answering `counts`; `identityOf` names a listed arrival whose identity it notes, `identityIsSeqOf` one whose seq, as bare text, is the identity); `note` may name the `leaf` its segment resumed; `park` (parks.commit with `{ kind: \"wait\", waitId }` at `address`); `commitSegment` (parks.commitSegment of the run: `resumed`, `joins` (none when absent) as `{ frame, pending }`, and `parks`, each at its `address` on the wait its `wait` names or, with `wakeAt` (milliseconds from now), a timer; `fence` names a lease; `settle`, when given, is the status the run is settled to in the same write, with an empty outcome; `owes` the frames of the races it owes (`owedRaces`, each with a null state); `settles` the frame of the race it settled (`settledRace`); `wakes` the wakes it answers, in any order; `refused`: the store fails it, `leaseLost`: the lease is lost, and either way nothing is written); `owed` (parks.owedRaces of the run, answering the frames of `races`, oldest first); `status` (runs.get of the run, answering a row of that `status`); `pendingJoins` (joins.hasPendingJoins of the run, answering `pending`); `claim` (parks.claimLeaf of the leaf at `address`, which must be parked); `finish` (parks.finishLeaf of the leaf at `address`, no fence); `lapse` (leases.claim of the run, as a process does after the one resuming its leaf died: a leaf left resuming is parked again); `deleteLeaves` (parks.deleteLeaves); `deleteFrames` (joins.deleteFrames of `frames`); `drop` (leases.dropRunState); `lease` (leases.claim of the run for `ttlMs`, a minute when absent, kept as `as`: it keeps the arrival mark now); `sweep` (waits.sweep of at most `limit`, answering `expect` swept: an arrival goes when no live wait on its record's edge has a mark below it and it is at or below the floor, the lowest mark an unexpired run lease took when it was claimed, else the latest seq, and at or below the mark `floor` names when the step names one; a wait its run opened is live while it exists, and one a delivery opened while its run exists or its `fire_event` row is queued); `keepDelivery` (inbound.keepDelivery of a delivery of no events, its one `fire_event` row named by `fire` and its `arrivals` logged under `resendWindowMs` as `log` does, opening `waits`, each `{ run, edge, key, preNoted?, as }` for that row's run (`preNoted` its trigger `{ identity, version? }`), kept by the name its `as` gives; it answers the mark before its arrivals, the one `arrivalMark` names); `start` (runs.start of the run `minted` names); `bury` (work.bury of the `fire_event` row `fire` names, claimed as the step's team's drain claims it: the waits a delivery opened for runs it queued that never started go with it); `completeKey` (work.completeKey of the `fire_event` row `fire` names, unclaimed, as a caller that ran the row itself completes it, answering `expect`: whether it was deleted; the waits a delivery opened under it for runs that never started go with it); `stranded` (waits.stranded of the run: `waits`, oldest stranded first, each `{ wait, edge, key, parked }`, `key` null for a wait opened without one, `parked` whether its leaf is still parked); `everyStranded` (waits.stranded across runs, `limit` per page, each page after the last wait of the page before, until a page is empty: the waits this case named, in the order listed, each `{ wait, run, edge, key, parked }`; waits it did not name are passed over, as a store the cases share keeps others).",
  "cases": [
    {
